NuvioMobile (core)
==================
StreamBridge’s runnable Android foundation is official NuvioMobile,
imported from:

  https://github.com/NuvioMedia/NuvioMobile
  branch: cmp-rewrite
  commit: d177eb57dfc8989e56de577bda8f4c2714b2bd64
  tag context: 0.4.17 (bump version; latest cmp-rewrite)
  previous pin: 465266d (0.4.16)
  license: GNU General Public License v3.0

Copyright (c) NuvioMedia and NuvioMobile contributors.

Imported as-is into `composeApp/`, `androidApp/`, `iosApp/` (version
config), and `gradle/` with StreamBridge identity overlays only
(applicationId, visible app name, launcher mark). Kotlin packages
remain `com.nuvio.app` / `com.nuvio.android`.

NuvioMobile-Enhanced (feature overlay)
======================================
Unique fork features (Live TV, OMDB episode ratings, hero trailer extras,
volume boost, HLS quality chooser, library calendar, profile insights,
download location / Wi-Fi-only, etc.) were overlaid from:

  https://github.com/luqmanfadlli/NuvioMobile-Enhanced
  branch: enhanced
  commit: d4a3b23
  license: GNU General Public License v3.0

Official NuvioMobile 0.4.17 plugin/sync/player fixes were re-applied on
top of that overlay. StreamBridge identity, empty default addons, and
updater source `sascio/MyBridge` are preserved.

Vendored Android binaries shipped by that pin (GPL application):

  composeApp/libs/lib-exoplayer-release.aar
  composeApp/libs/lib-decoder-ffmpeg-release.aar
  composeApp/libs/lib-decoder-av1-release.aar
  composeApp/libs/lib-decoder-mpegh-release.aar
  composeApp/libs/lib-ui-release.aar
  composeApp/libs/lib-nuvio-engine-android-0.1.1.aar
  composeApp/libs/quickjs-kt-android-1.0.5-nuvio.aar

Related upstream (not copied as source trees in Milestone 1):

  NuvioTV        https://github.com/NuvioMedia/NuvioTV        e7a335e
  nuvio-engine   https://github.com/NuvioMedia/nuvio-engine   772f8c0
                 (GPL-3.0-or-later; Android consumes the AAR above)


Historical StreamBridge client (quarantined)
============================================
`legacy/streambridge-app/` is the previous independent Android client
(custom Media3 player, original Compose UI). Those files were
originally published under the MIT License (see
`legacy/LICENSE-MIT.txt`). They are **not** on the runtime or CI path.

The combined StreamBridge distribution is GPL-3.0.
